<%# The turn is not over until the stream says so, and neither a long answer
    nor a slow tool says anything about itself while it is happening. This row
    is the page's "still working" — the state the TUI pins to its own edge.

    It belongs to the band above the composer, not to the timeline: the
    timeline is the record of what the turn did, and this row is the page
    saying it is not finished yet. In the flow it also pushed the last tool
    row up the screen every time the answer grew a line.

    Drawn once per turn. A turn started from the page gets this row in the
    answer to the POST that started it; a page opened on a turn already running
    draws it at first paint. A tool call does not re-send it: the row would
    arrive identical, and the replacement only made the text flash.

    Delegated runs are not drawn here. They outlive the turn that asked for
    them, so they are read in the footer's sheet (see _subagent_sheet): one
    place for them, and a page that is idle still shows the run that is
    working. -%>
<div class="working-band" id="working">
  <p class="row working" data-since="<%= h(since) %>" data-threshold="0">
    <span class="mark working" aria-hidden="true"><%= mark(:working) %></span>
    <span class="label">Working…</span>
    <span class="live-clock"></span>
  </p>
</div>
